  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A student is provided with a variable voltage source&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math>, a test resistor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#937;</mi></math>, two identical galvanometers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and two additional resistors, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>M</mi><mi>&#937;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>001</mn><mi>&#937;</mi></math>. For conducting an experiment to verify ohm&#39;s law, the most suitable circuit is:</p>",
    "image": null
  },
